description:
The Russian major is a liberal arts program designed to give students a thorough grounding in the language and a familiarity with Russian literature and culture. It can also prepare students for a career in government or in the private sector, for graduate work in Russian language, literature, and culture, and for professional schools.

Students who major in Russian will:
- attain an advanced level of proficiency in all four language skills (speaking, listening, reading, writing);
- gain a comprehensive knowledge of the masterpieces of 19th and 20th century Russian literature and of their historical context;
- achieve an in-depth understanding of contemporary Russian culture, as well as the historical and cultural traditions that have shaped it.
